        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Virginia conducted both 45 days of early voting and election day voting.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "By 7 p.m. on election day, the total number of ballots cast in Virginia was known precisely.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The total number of votes cast includes both early votes and mail-in votes.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "It is possible to determine how many additional votes remain to be counted after election day.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Once a candidate crosses a certain vote threshold, their opponent cannot catch up regardless of remaining votes.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "The process of reporting election results is often misrepresented as ongoing rather than a matter of awaiting final tallies.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
