        "text": "The accuracy and completeness of Virginia's vote counting system is trustworthy.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Knowing the total number of votes cast enables reliable prediction of electoral outcomes based on remaining votes.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Election news media coverage tends to exaggerate uncertainty by framing delayed results as suspenseful events.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "Early voting and mail-in voting are treated equivalently in the official vote count.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "Voters in Virginia trust that their ballots will be accurately accounted for and included in totals.",
