    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92596.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 32,
    "turn_text": "do if this doesn't work and what do we do if this doesn't work? Whereas it seems so often now it's, here is our position, dammit, and we don't have a backup, whether it's because we have a 80, 20 district back home and they're not going to accept us if we compromise or whether it is some kind of ideological ossification. But the idea of you know, giving something to get the bulk of the legislation through, I don't want to say it's a law start because you've done it, but it seems to be like it's, it's certainly less highly pursued than it used to be.",
