    "turn_idx": 38,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. And it's interesting, even on the political side in the campaigns, a big attack is, oh, if If anyone ever listening turns them on a television in Washington, DC area, they would see, oh, Spanberger votes with Pelosi 100% of the time. Well, what is totally inherently lost in whatever numbers they're throwing out is that if you look at Kevin McCarthy's number, the minority leader of the outgoing house, or you look at a whole array of different Republicans, I vote with them a whole heck of a lot of the time. We actually agree on a lot of things. Now, unfortunately, not some of the major things. And so it's legislation that we vote on every day and here and there that moves forward without little fanfare, because it's kind of the nuts and bolts of governing. But it's interesting to me that there's just this notion that everything's binary. If you agree with a Democrat, you disagree with a Republican. And there's a general assessment and acceptance that that's the case. And into that kind of 80-20 Ronald Reagan quote, there's plenty of people that I can work with. Like, you know, there's a wonderful outgoing member of Congress, Congressman McKinley from West Virginia, where, you know, he's pretty, pretty conservative. We have very, very different political backgrounds and priorities across the board. But we agree on protecting rural health systems and clinics. And we actually just got a tremendous piece of legislation signed into law called the Summer Barrow Prevention Treatment and Recovery Act. That is, I believe, an incredibly important piece of legislation to help those struggling with addiction and substance use disorder. Now, are we ever going to do, he's leaving Congress, but if you were saying, you know, there's probably a hundred different things that we would never work on together.",
