    "turn_text": "I have made the joke and people would say, oh, no, no, but I do think there's a level of truth to it. This was in the post-9-11 hiring surge. For those who don't know in the role that I was hired into, There's a maximum age of 37, because it's mandatory retirement at 57. Occasionally, there's a waiver here or there. And so I was far younger than that at the time. And so I kind of joked, I had romance languages in German, and I was young enough that I could easily be put on the back burner. And so I think that that was it. I also had been, I substituted at an embassy school in the US, but I was a long-term sub at the Islamic Saudi Academy in northern Virginia, which teaches a lot of diplomats' children. And so I think that by virtue of that, I had some ties that I think they just needed to ensure that I really was a substitute teacher, et cetera. And then I had spent all that time in Germany. I had lived in Hamburg during the time. Unfortunately that the 11 bombers have been there. So I don't know. I think it was really I was young and I spoke Relatively boring languages and got moved to the bottom of the file.",
