    "turn_text": "necessarily seeing the back and forth. And so there might be places where, you know, you did something really well that they didn't actually even see or there might be place where in the end it turned out fine, but it's because they saved the day and you didn't actually even, you know, you didn't see that they made up the difference on some sort of shortcoming you had. And so I just think that that's probably my biggest lesson learned is that just always doing that secondary assessment It doesn't mean you can't, when things go well, you can't celebrate the successes. But when you're in, when you do that, it makes it easier when things are actually in a troubling bad circumstance.",
