    "turn_idx": 140,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. Yeah. And I would agree. And I think that, you know, one of the things that I'm, I'm proud of is that the legislation, you know, the sort of brass tacks of the job that I've worked on. If you had, you know, when I was first running for Congress, of course, you know, the cost of healthcare, the cost of prescription drugs, there's certain things that are universal concerns. And I would walk in any room and if not given the opportunity based on a schedule to talk to people first, there are certain kind of top lines that I would always discuss because they matter to everybody. Sometimes they, you know, the cost of prescription drugs might impact people in different ways, but it matters to everybody. And what I loved along the campaign trail in the seventh district of Virginia, and we've been impacted pretty significantly by redistricting, but the common thread of the old seventh and the new seventh is the landmass wise, majority of rural, majority agricultural population, majority suburban. So I can walk into five to five events in a day. I'm walking into five very different places. You know,",
