    "turn_text": "Okay. So not realistic at all at all, but I used to work. I used to have an asset. So someone who was providing valuable information to the United States about his home country who loved that show. Oh, and so I didn't necessarily make time to watch covert affairs. But whenever I was gonna go out on a meeting with him, I would go to whatever the summary of shows, I don't know if it's Wikipedia or wherever you find those things, and read the summary of each individual episode so that when I would go meet him, we could sit down and he would chit chat about, oh did you see this one? And so I had like a major working knowledge of the show that I had maybe only ever seen like one episode of. And it was so funny to me that here's a man coming from a country where he was really risking his life by meeting with me if he had ever been found out. He would",
